WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
Welcome to Grade 2 English, Unit 7: The World Around Us.

2
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:11.300
In this unit you learn about the world around us — the plants,
the trees, the air, and the land and water we all share.

3
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.420
You find out how to care for planet Earth by
planting, watering, picking up litter and recycling.

4
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.300
You learn the parts of a plant
and why trees keep our air clean,

5
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.080
and you practise saying thank you
for the beautiful things in nature.

6
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:31.960
By the end you can make your own promise to care
for the Earth, just like Amal in this unit's story,

7
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.000
“Amal and the Little Tree”.

8
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:40.340
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:47.520
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
describe ways to care for the environment, including planting,

10
00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:50.040
watering, picking up litter and recycling.

11
00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.580
You will also name the parts of a
plant and say what each part does.

12
00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:58.840
You will also explain why plants and
trees are important for clean air.

13
00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.140
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.160
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: boat, coat, soap, snow, grow, show.

15
00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:13.640
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

16
00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:18.520
The reading sequence includes Mother
Earth Day and Plants and Clean Air.

17
00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:23.700
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

18
00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.840
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

19
00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:33.420
The first language focus is Present
Continuous: Actions Happening Now.

20
00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.760
We use the present continuous to
say what is happening right now.

21
00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:43.040
In this unit it lets you describe what people
are doing to help the Earth, such as planting,

22
00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.680
watering or picking up litter.

23
00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:48.440
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

24
00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:53.560
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1 — Talk About Environmental Actions.

25
00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:56.840
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

26
00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:03.140
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

27
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.020
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:10.160
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

29
00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:16.600
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
